From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <81541646+RyanTheTide@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 07:47:50 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] tests: Add ext-session-lock-v1 tests

Read back every frame of every view from its onscreen framebuffer and
count a frame painted while the session is locked as a leak if it has
any pixel other than the black blank and the lock surfaces (the
compositor-drawn pointer sprite excepted). Every test asserts there
were none.

Cover lock and unlock (locked only after a blanked frame was presented,
keyboard and pointer focus on the lock surface, both back on the
window after unlock), a monitor plugged in and out while locked (blank
from its first frame, then its own lock surface), a keyboard plugged in
while locked, a lock client that goes away while locked (stays locked
and blank until a new lock client unlocks), a second lock while one is
held (finished), a lock destroyed before locked (given up) and the
protocol errors.

MUTTER_SESSION_LOCK_DUMP_DIR saves the read back frames as PNGs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
